// markdownlint-cli2 configuration — gate #17 of the 2026-08-27 conventions
// plan. Run by tests/quality/markdown.test.mjs and by the `lint` CI job.
//
// THE CORPUS IS DEFINED HERE, ONCE. Both callers invoke the tool with no
// arguments so the test and CI cannot drift apart about what is linted;
// markdown.test.mjs asserts these globs verbatim.
//
// docs/plans/** is excluded because a plan is true as of its date. Rewriting
// an archive so a linter goes green falsifies a record.
//
// src/, tools/ and scripts/ markdown are IN. The brief for this gate named
// only docs/ and the root, which was right when it was written — then P4
// landed twelve per-domain README.md files under src/, tools/ci/ and
// scripts/, and they would have sat outside every markdown check while
// looking covered. Adding them cost nothing: measured 2026-08-27, all twelve
// pass the tuned rule set with zero issues, taking the corpus from 35 files
// to 47.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// TUNING RECORD (measured 2026-08-27 over 34 documents, defaults, 6,106 hits)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The rule was: disable MD013/MD033/MD041 per the plan, plus any rule firing
// more than 50 times — a rule that fires 4,956 times is not finding defects,
// it is describing a house style this repo does not have. Everything else
// stays on and its violations were FIXED, not disabled.
//
//   MD013 line-length            4956  disabled by the plan. Prettier owns
//                                      wrapping; two tools with opinions
//                                      about line width start a churn war.
//   MD040 fenced-code-language    409  >50. Many fences here hold TAP output,
//                                      log excerpts and shell transcripts
//                                      that have no language tag to give.
//   MD024 no-duplicate-heading    186  >50. The code chapters repeat section
//                                      names ("What it does", "Gotchas") per
//                                      module on purpose — that repetition is
//                                      the navigation.
//   MD028 no-blanks-blockquote    160  >50. Multi-paragraph blockquotes are
//                                      how the incident write-ups quote a
//                                      source and then comment on it.
//   MD036 no-emphasis-as-heading  132  >50. Bold lead-ins inside a section
//                                      are used as emphasis, not as headings,
//                                      and promoting them would wreck the
//                                      heading tree this file keeps checking.
//   MD010 no-hard-tabs             89  >50. Tabs appear inside fenced blocks
//                                      that reproduce real output verbatim.
//   MD025 single-title             61  >50. Several documents legitimately
//                                      restart at H1 per major part.
//   MD033 no-inline-html           12  disabled by the plan (<!-- fact:ID -->
//                                      style markers and <br> in tables).
//   MD041 first-line-heading        0  disabled by the plan; fires nowhere
//                                      today, kept off so a front-matter
//                                      document does not become a failure.
//
// TWO MORE ARE OFF, AND NOT FOR NOISE — THEY LOSE TO PRETTIER.
// Prettier is the formatter of record here (CLAUDE.md hard rule 8: a
// PostToolUse hook runs it on every edited document, and you do not fight its
// formatting). Where the two tools disagree about the same bytes, the loop is
// infinite and the gate is unfixable, so the disagreement is settled here
// once, in prettier's favour, rather than by whoever ran a tool last:
//   MD030 list-marker-space   prettier emits `1.  item` (two spaces) for
//                             ordered lists; markdownlint --fix rewrites it to
//                             one, and prettier puts it back. Measured as a
//                             ping-pong on docs/code/00-file-index.md.
//   MD049 emphasis-style      prettier ALTERNATES delimiters for nested
//                             emphasis — `_"... *without* ..."_` — which is
//                             correct markdown and which MD049 cannot express,
//                             since it wants one delimiter everywhere.
//   MD060 table-column-style  both tools align table pipes and they disagree
//                             about the display width of angle-bracket text.
//                             Measured on docs/operate/01-commands.md, a row
//                             holding `jobs/<slug>/`: prettier --check calls
//                             the file clean, MD060 wants the pipe one column
//                             over. MD033 is off, so `<slug>` is prose here,
//                             not HTML — and prettier is the tool that
//                             actually rewrites the file.
//
// TWO FILES ARE OUT OF THE CORPUS, for the same reason docs-links.test.mjs
// exempts them: docs/measurements.md and docs/roster-log.md are dated
// archives. Editing an archive so a linter goes green falsifies a record.
//
// STILL ON, and this is the half that makes the gate worth running:
// MD001 heading-increment, MD029 ol-prefix, MD031 blanks-around-fences,
// MD038 no-space-in-code, MD056 table-column-count, MD051 link-fragments,
// MD014 commands-show-output, MD026, and every other default.
//
// They found 101 defects on the first run and every one was FIXED, not
// disabled. Two were worth the whole exercise:
//   * MD051 caught `[Part 2](#part-2--scriptsleadsenrichmjs)` — an anchor
//     still pointing at the pre-re-layout heading. A link the sweep missed.
//   * MD056 caught six table rows holding an unescaped `|` inside a code span
//     (regexes like `/(?:^|\s)--file/`). The renderer reads that pipe as a
//     cell separator and DROPS the rest of the row, so the documented regex
//     was being displayed truncated. Now escaped.
{
  "globs": [
    "docs/**/*.md",
    "*.md",
    "src/**/*.md",
    "tools/**/*.md",
    "scripts/**/*.md",
    "!docs/plans/**",
    "!docs/measurements.md",
    "!docs/roster-log.md",
  ],
  "config": {
    "MD013": false,
    "MD033": false,
    "MD041": false,
    "MD040": false,
    "MD024": false,
    "MD028": false,
    "MD036": false,
    "MD010": false,
    "MD025": false,
    "MD030": false,
    "MD049": false,
    "MD060": false,
  },
}
